Decision Rationale:
According to SOP Section 5.1.6, applications with debt-to-income ratios "significantly exceeding maximum permissible levels" generate "Not Qualified" designations. The applicant's DTI of 59.51% exceeds the institutional maximum threshold of 50% for Qualified Mortgage compliance (SOP Section 3). Despite strong compensating factors (excellent credit, substantial assets, stable employment), the DTI exceeds the absolute maximum threshold, resulting in a decline decision per institutional policy.

The application will not proceed to underwriting phase as it failed prequalification screening. All required verifications and validations were completed in accordance with the SOP, and the decision is documented with appropriate audit trail.

Note: This application was previously processed and declined on 2025-12-16. The current processing confirms the original decision was correct per SOP guidelines.
