a. Key points of the SOP:
1. The SOP establishes a comprehensive framework for mortgage loan origination, covering intake, pre-qualification, credit underwriting, property valuation, and final decision.
2. The process is divided into three main phases: Mortgage Application Intake and Pre-qualification (5.1), Credit Underwriting (5.2), and Property Valuation and Appraisal (5.3).
3. Key steps include: identity verification (5.1.1), employment/income validation (5.1.2), asset validation (5.1.3), credit consent and report pulling (5.1.4), credit score calculation using tri-merge middle score methodology (5.1.5), pre-qualification screening (5.1.6), max loan amount calculation (5.1.7), detailed employment verification (5.2.1-5.2.3), credit analysis (5.2.4), DTI/DSCR calculation (5.2.5), probability of default scoring (5.2.6), interest rate determination (5.2.7), compensating factors analysis (5.2.8), underwriting summary (5.2.9), appraisal ordering (5.3.1), property inspection (5.3.2), comparable analysis (5.3.3), value reconciliation (5.3.4), AVM validation (5.3.5), LTV recalculation (5.3.6), final decision rendering (5.4.1-5.4.4), and compliance monitoring (5.4.6-5.4.7).
4. Outputs include: prequalification decision, max loan amount, estimated interest rate, verified income, DTI ratio, DSCR, probability of default score, credit score grade, final interest rate, appraised value, LTV ratio, final decision, conditions count, etc.

