<analysis>
The VerifyEmploymentAndIncome tool returned an error: "Cannot verify income for Not Qualified applications". This confirms that the system enforces the SOP requirement that applications with "Not Qualified" pre-qualification decisions cannot proceed to full underwriting verification.

The re-retrieved application data confirms the current status remains "Not Qualified" with all previous data unchanged.

According to SOP 5.1.6: "The resulting preliminary_DTI is evaluated against institutional thresholds, with ratios significantly exceeding maximum permissible levels generating 'Not Qualified' designations..."

The calculated DTI of 95.97% is more than double the maximum permissible back-end DTI of 43% for Qualified Mortgage compliance. This is clearly a "significantly exceeding" case.

SOP 5.1.7 states: "For applications receiving 'Qualified' or 'Conditionally Qualified' designations, the system shall calculate max_loan_amount_prequalified..." This application has a negative max loan amount, further confirming it should not proceed.

The application appears to have inconsistent processing - property valuation activities (appraisal ordered, site inspection) were conducted despite the "Not Qualified" pre-qualification. This may represent a process deviation.

Next step: According to the SOP, applications with "Not Qualified" designations should not proceed further. The appropriate action would be to render a final decline decision based on the pre-qualification failure.
</analysis>

