However, SOP 5.1.6 states: "ratios significantly exceeding maximum permissible levels generating 'Not Qualified' designations, ratios moderately exceeding standard thresholds generating 'Conditionally Qualified' designations requiring compensating factors, and ratios within acceptable ranges generating 'Qualified' designations, though cases falling near threshold boundaries may require judgment regarding which classification is most appropriate given the overall risk profile."

The DTI of 53.88% is 10.88 percentage points above the 43% threshold. This appears to be "significantly exceeding" rather than "moderately exceeding." However, the application has substantial compensating factors that may warrant exception consideration.
