<final_response>
Application MLN-2025-063003 has been processed according to the Standard Operating Procedure. After comprehensive analysis following all required phases (Mortgage Application Intake and Pre-qualification, Credit Underwriting, and Property Valuation), the application has been declined.

**Key Decision Factors:**
- **Debt-to-Income Ratio**: 50.16% (exceeds maximum threshold of 43%)
- **Probability of Default Score**: 8.83% (exceeds threshold for automatic referral)
- **Compensating Factors**: 9 points total, but insufficient to offset elevated risk indicators

**Application Strengths:**
- Excellent credit profile (FICO 785, no derogatory marks)
- Strong employment history (11 years at Ochsner Health System)
- Substantial liquid assets ($95,000) and retirement accounts ($185,000)
- Excellent property condition with adequate comparables

**Final Decision Rationale:**
Despite strong individual credit factors, the elevated debt burden relative to income (DTI of 50.16%) creates unacceptable risk exposure that exceeds institutional thresholds. The Probability of Default score of 8.83% indicates elevated statistical likelihood of default within 36 months. Compensating factors, while present, are not sufficient to justify an exception to standard underwriting guidelines.

The application has been processed in compliance with all applicable federal regulations including ECOA, TILA, HMDA, and Dodd-Frank requirements. All required documentation and verification procedures have been completed according to the Standard Operating Procedure.

**Decision**: DECLINED
**Decision Date**: 2025-12-16
**Underwriter**: UW-6527
</final_response>[0m

