2. The process begins with identity verification (KYC), employment/income validation, asset verification, credit report acquisition, and pre-qualification screening.
3. Credit underwriting involves detailed verification of employment/income, assets, credit history analysis, DTI/DSCR calculations, probability of default scoring, credit grading, interest rate determination, and compensating factors analysis.
4. Property valuation includes ordering appraisals, conducting inspections, comparable sales analysis, AVM validation, and LTV calculation.
5. Final decision rendering synthesizes all findings into approval/decline decisions with conditions.
6. Outputs include prequalification decision, verified income, ratios, scores, grades, interest rates, appraised value, LTV, final decision, and various metrics.
