responded: <sop_analysis>
a. Key points of the SOP:
1. The SOP establishes a comprehensive framework for mortgage loan origination, credit assessment, collateral valuation, and decisioning.
2. It consists of three main phases: Mortgage Application Intake and Pre-qualification (5.1), Credit Underwriting (5.2), and Property Valuation and Appraisal (5.3), followed by Final Decision Rendering (5.4).
3. The process begins with a completed Uniform Residential Loan Application with specific required fields (applicant_name, applicant_ssn, applicant_dob, applicant_address, property_address, property_type, property_occupancy, estimated_property_value, requested_loan_amount, down_payment_amount, loan_purpose, loan_term_months, employment_status, employer_name, employment_years, gross_monthly_income, additional_income_monthly, liquid_assets, retirement_accounts, credit_consent_signed, credit_consent_timestamp, pay_stubs_uploaded, tax_returns_uploaded, w2_forms_uploaded, bank_statements_uploaded).
4. The first step is to retrieve the application data using the application_id (MLN-2025-063024) to verify all required input fields are present.
5. The SOP requires sequential execution: identity verification (5.1.1), employment/income validation (5.1.2), asset validation (5.1.3), credit consent and report pulling (5.1.4), credit score determination and debt calculation (5.1.5), pre-qualification screening (5.1.6), pre-qualification letter generation (5.1.7).
6. Then proceed to underwriting: employment/income verification (5.2.1-5.2.2), asset verification (5.2.3), credit analysis (5.2.4), DTI/DSCR calculation (5.2.5), probability of default scoring (5.2.6), interest rate determination (5.2.7), compensating factors analysis (5.2.8), underwriting summary (5.2.9).
