The SOP states in 5.1.6: "ratios significantly exceeding maximum permissible levels generating 'Not Qualified' designations, ratios moderately exceeding standard thresholds generating 'Conditionally Qualified' designations requiring compensating factors, and ratios within acceptable ranges generating 'Qualified' designations". 

The DTI of 71.02% is not "moderately exceeding" - it's significantly exceeding the 43% threshold. However, the application has strong compensating factors: 
